Found the loop. Lines 437-471 show the restart loop:

```typescript
const supervisor = detectRespawnSupervisor(process.env);
// ...
while (true) {
  try {
    await startLoop();
    break;
  } catch (err) {
    const isGatewayAlreadyRunning = ...;
    if (!supervisor || !isGatewayAlreadyRunning) {
      throw err;  // <-- This throws out of the loop!
    }
    // otherwise retry
  }
}
```

The problem: when `assertValidGatewayStartupConfigSnapshot` throws inside `startLoop`, the error propagates up. If `supervisor` is null/undefined (not supervised by systemd), the error is thrown out and the process exits. 

If `supervisor` is detected (systemd), the error gets swallowed and the loop retries indefinitely—that's the crash loop. The fix is to detect consecutive startup failures and exit after N attempts instead of looping forever.

